  "notes": "{押|お}す is a godan verb meaning to push, press, or stamp.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: {押|お}される (passive, to be pushed)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦ボタン→ボタン：02963_botan⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{押|お}す: to press a button\n- ⟦{扉|とびら}→扉：04494_tobira⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{押|お}す: to push a door\n- ⟦ハンコ→判子：00089_hanko⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{押|お}す: to stamp a seal\n- ⟦{印鑑|いんかん}→印鑑：05290_inkan⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{押|お}す: to affix one's seal\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n⟦{引|ひ}く→引く：01978_hiku⟧ (to pull)\n\nDOOR SIGNS:\n- {押|お}す: Push\n- ⟦{引|ひ}く→引く：01978_hiku⟧: Pull\n\nUSAGE:\nStamping a seal (⟦{判子|はんこ}→判子：00089_hanko⟧/⟦{印鑑|いんかん}→印鑑：05290_inkan⟧) is common in Japan for official documents instead of signatures.",
